    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe requirement: `GET /api/owners/{id}` should return `contactPreference = 'EMAIL'` when an email is present, otherwise `'PHONE'`.\n\nI implemented this as a read-time derived field, mirroring the existing `locality` field pattern:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema (the response model), which regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field/getter/setter.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that derives the value: `\"EMAIL\"` when the owner's email is non-null and non-blank, `\"PHONE\"` otherwise.\n\nBoth acceptance tests pass (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite reports `BUILD SUCCESS` with no failures or errors.",
